000450820018000530900019000711000021000902450100001112600065002113000018002765201021002946500021013156500025013366500028013616500016013896500029014056500028014344914820/8/2019  a9781633693647  aDHSPKT  aEng  223a658.402 2  a658.4022bJ661  aJohnson, Whitney  aBuild an a team:bplay to their strengths and lead them up the learning curve/cWhitney Johnson  aBoston, Massachusetts:bHarvard Business Review Press,c2018  a194p.;c21cm.  aDo you want to have a high-performing team that strives for greatness, even in the face of uncertainty? Do you want to be a boss people love, while also driving high performance? Building morale and high performance are about engagement, and engagement is all about learning, argues Whitney Johnson. In over twenty years of research, investing, consulting, and coaching, Johnson has seen that people need continuous learning and fresh challenges to stay engaged. In this book you'll learn how to build an "A" team by leading team members on their current learning curve, how to design their jobs to maximize learning and engagement, and how to implement a seven-step process for advancing up the learning curve. We all want opportunities to learn, experiment, and grow in our jobs. The best bosses know this, and they know how to make it happen through thoughtful role design and just enough challenge. The result is a team that learns how to thrive, no matter what the industry throws at themcProvided by publisher  aEmployee morale.  aEmployee motivation.  aEngagement (Philosophy)  aManagement.  aOrganizational learning.  aTeams in the workplace.00440nam a2200169 a 4500001000600000005000900006020001800015040001100033041000800044082001800052090001900070245004000089260006400129300002200193650002600215650002900241496115/9/2019  a9781633692787  aDHSPKT  aEng  223a658.312 8  a658.3128bH431  aHBR guide to performance management  aBoston, Masachusetts:bHarvard Business Review Press,c2017  aix, 244p.